{"case_id":"C092","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":99,"change_types":["implementation_refactor","explicit_integer_cast"],"affected_functions":["wuffs_base__pixel_buffer__set_color_u32_at"],"reason":"The commit only introduces a temporary `bgr565` value and explicitly casts it to `uint16_t` before the same `wuffs_base__store_u16le` call. It does not add or modify an entry point, protocol, initialization/state requirement, configuration, or input constraint. The existing GIF harness still exercises the high-level image-decoding path with a configured pixel buffer, while the zlib harness is unaffected. Therefore, the source change alone does not create a fuzz-harness maintenance need.","evidence":["The BGR_565 case computes the same expression `(b5 << 0) | (g6 << 5) | (r5 << 11)` as before.","The destination remains `row + (2 * ((size_t)x))`, and storage still uses `wuffs_base__store_u16le`.","The only behavioral-form change is an explicit `(uint16_t)bgr565` conversion; no public API or calling convention changes appear in the diff.","`gif_fuzzer.c` already invokes `wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_image_config`, creates a pixel buffer with `wuffs_base__pixel_buffer__set_from_slice`, and decodes frames through `wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame`.","`zlib_fuzzer.c` targets zlib transformation and has no relationship to the changed pixel-color storage code."],"recommended_action":"No harness update is required for this commit; retain the existing fuzz targets."}
